# The default services of a Luna Linux user session.
#
# They work thanks to uwsm: it brings the session up in a way that lets systemd
# reach graphical-session.target, which the units below are bound to. That is
# why the panel and the notifications are not launched from the Hyprland
# config - systemd runs them and restarts them if they die.
#
# The preset is applied by systemctl --user preset-all. In case nobody ever ran
# that, the package also ships symlinks in
# /usr/lib/systemd/user/graphical-session.target.wants, which makes the set
# work immediately and for any user.
enable waybar.service
enable mako.service
# The wallpaper is set by swaybg through luna-wallpaper rather than hyprpaper:
# that one crashes without working EGL, which means in any virtual machine.
enable luna-wallpaper.service
enable hypridle.service
enable hyprpolkitagent.service
enable cliphist.service
# blueman-applet is deliberately left out: without a bluetooth adapter the unit
# simply fails and spoils the failed-service count on the panel. Anyone who
# wants the applet can run
# systemctl --user enable --now blueman-applet.service
